{"v":"3.0.0","project":{"accession":"PRJNA1478350","title":"Fe(III)-mediated Fe-S mineral formation retains sulfur-derived reductive capacity after autotrophic Cr(VI) bioreduction","description":"varying Fe2O3 dosages did not substantially alter the proportional distribution of major phyla among these biosystems, indicating that Fe2O3 exerted limited influence on community structure. The relative abundance analysis further confirmed this trend (Fig. 3e). Proteobacteria increased markedly from 42.31% in the inoculum to 73.19% in the control and 66.24%-71.90% in the Fe2O3 treatments. In contrast, Bacteroidota decreased from 21.47% in the inoculum to 7.10% in the control and 6.51%-8.55% in the Fe2O3 treatments. At the genus level (Fig. 3f), Thiobacillus and Thermomonas were significantly enriched in all operated bioreactors. Thiobacillus increased from 1.03% in the inoculum to 27.41% in the control and 23.84%-29.25% in the Fe2O3 amended systems.","organism":null,"data_type":"Raw sequence reads","center_name":"China University of Geosciences (beijing)","submission_date":"2026/06/15 00:00","last_update":null},"sample_cols":["accession","title","collection_date","country","region","city","lat","lon","urban_status","urban_context","eligibility_reason","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","host","location_resolution","country_iso2","place_id","location_status","location_method","location_note","geo_loc_raw","collection_year"],"samples":[["SAMN60879181","Metagenome or environmental sample from activated sludge metagenome","2025-10-20","China","Beijing","Beijing",39.0,116.0,"non_environmental",null,"laboratory or culture material","bioreactor",null,null,null,"laboratory","coordinate","CN",1816670,"probable","text","region's main city","China: Beijing",2025],["SAMN60879183","Metagenome or environmental sample from activated sludge metagenome","2025-10-20","China","Beijing","Beijing",39.0,116.0,"non_environmental",null,"laboratory or culture mater